# Payload Client Provider


## What is a client provider?

A client provider is a layer around the frontend that makes contact with the backend. It makes contact once for a shared SDK instance, using the context API from Svelte so it can be accessed everywhere.

## Why use the client provider?

So that you can have a centralized payload fetch configuration and reuse the client throughout components, and have it preloaded once for reusing.

## Install SDK

Install this in the frontend.

```bash
pnpm add @payloadcms/sdk
```

**Where to place the provider**

Place this at your app root (top-level layout or `App`) so it's initialized once and available globally. Store it in a `providers` or `lib/providers` folder and import it into the root.

## Client provider component

This example creates a single shared Payload SDK client and exposes it via Svelte context (`PAYLOAD_CLIENT_CONTEXT`). It accepts `apiBase`, an optional `fetchFn`, and `children`, and provides helper methods such as `request`, `switchToJWT` and `createServerClient` for client and server side use. Place this provider at the app root so the client is instantiated once and shared across the app. Use `usePayloadProvider()` in components to read the provider from context it returns the provider instance or throws a clear error if the provider is not available.

```html
<script context="module" lang="ts">
  import { setContext, getContext } from 'svelte';
  import { createPayloadClient } from '$lib/payloadClient';

  export const PAYLOAD_CLIENT_CONTEXT = Symbol('payloadClientContext');

  export class PayloadClientProvider {
    client = $state<any>();
    apiBase = $state<string>('');
    fetchOptions = $state<RequestInit>({ credentials: 'include' });

    constructor(apiBase?: string, fetchFn: typeof fetch = fetch) {
      if (apiBase) this.apiBase = apiBase;
      this.client = createPayloadClient({ fetchFn, baseUrl: this.apiBase });
    }

    updateFetchOptions(options: RequestInit) {
      this.fetchOptions = { ...this.fetchOptions, ...options };
      this.client = createPayloadClient({
        fetchFn: (input, init) => fetch(input, { ...init, ...this.fetchOptions }),
        baseUrl: this.apiBase
      });
    }

    async request(args: Parameters<ReturnType<typeof createPayloadClient>['request']>[0]) {
      return this.client.request(args);
    }

    switchToJWT(token: string) {
      this.updateFetchOptions({
        headers: {
          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
          ...(this.fetchOptions.headers as Record<string, string> | undefined)
        }
      });
    }

    static createServerClient(token?: string) {
      return createPayloadClient({ baseUrl: undefined, token });
    }
  }

  export const usePayloadProvider = () => {
    const provider = getContext<PayloadClientProvider>(PAYLOAD_CLIENT_CONTEXT);
    if (!provider) {
      throw new Error('PayloadClientProvider not found');
    }
    return provider;
  };
</script>

<script lang="ts">
  import type { Snippet } from 'svelte';

  let {
    apiBase,
    fetchFn,
    children
  }: {
    apiBase: string;
    fetchFn?: typeof fetch;
    children?: Snippet;
  } = $props();

  const client = $bindable(new PayloadClientProvider(apiBase, fetchFn));
  setContext(PAYLOAD_CLIENT_CONTEXT, client);
</script>

{@render children?.()}
```

**Preparing the Provider**

Import this provider at your app root so it initializes once and wraps the UI. Example: import and wrap your root component with the provider (see code below). Doing so guarantees a single client instance is reused across pages and components. Components can then call `usePayloadProvider()` to access the shared client; the helper throws if the provider hasn't been set in context.
```html
<script lang="ts">
  import PayloadClient from '$lib/providers/payloadProvider.svelte';
  import UserProvider from '$lib/providers/userProvider.svelte';
  import '../app.css';

  let { children, data } = $props();
</script>

<PayloadClient>
  <UserProvider
    initialUser={data?.user}
    loginExpireTimestamp={data?.loginExpireTimestamp}
  >
    {@render children()}
  </UserProvider>
</PayloadClient>
```

